WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.260
doubleValues gives each thread two elements, separated by blockDim.x.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:13.095
Each assignment needs a loaded input before its multiply. main sets threads from warpsPerBlock and allocates twice as many elements.

00:00:13.095 --> 00:00:18.095
The teaching trace models this dependency, not compiler instruction order.

00:00:19.595 --> 00:00:20.430
Load.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.860
A warp requests its input values.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.690
Wait or issue another warp.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.885
Only instructions with ready operands can issue.

00:00:27.885 --> 00:00:29.410
Multiply and store.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.940
Use the returned values and write results.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.690
An SM keeps resident warps and their register values available.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:42.905
A warp scheduler selects a ready instruction for an appropriate execution unit.

00:00:42.905 --> 00:00:46.550
Another warp can issue while a load dependency blocks the first.
